@startuml Error Handling

!define C4Container
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/plantuml-stdlib/C4-PlantUML/master/C4_Container.puml

title Error Handling - Sequence Diagram

participant "Frontend\n[Container: Vue.js]" as Frontend
participant "Backend API\n[Container: FastAPI]" as Backend
database "PostgreSQL\n[Container: Database]" as Database
participant "Worker\n[Container: Python]" as Worker
participant "OpenStack\n[External System]" as OpenStack

note across
  Nothing is retried automatically. A half-applied OpenTofu run is not
  something to repeat blindly, so every failure ends in a FAILED task
  that a person looks at.
end note

== Case 1: the job itself fails ==

activate Worker
Worker -> Worker: catch Exception
note right
  Raised by any step of the
  Background Task Execution:
  git clone, Packer build,
  tofu init / plan / apply.
end note

Worker -> Worker: collect_terraform_outputs()
note right
  Best effort: a half-finished apply
  still created resources, and their
  outputs describe what exists.
end note

alt terraform dir exists
    Worker -> OpenStack: tofu destroy\n(variables without file payloads)
    activate OpenStack
    note right
      Best-effort cleanup of a partially
      applied graph, so orphaned networks,
      ports and volumes do not quietly eat
      the project's quota. Failures here
      are logged and ignored — the task
      fails either way.
    end note
    OpenStack --> Worker: resources removed\n(or cleanup failed)
    deactivate OpenStack
end

Worker -> Worker: shred per-task clouds.yaml\n+ cleanup_repository()

Worker -> Worker: raise Failure(\nmessage, deployment_id,\nlogs_dict, commit_info,\nterraform_outputs)

Worker -> Worker: job_queue.failure_columns(error)
note right
  The Failure carries what the job
  produced before it broke. No event
  bus and no regex over a traceback:
  the columns are built directly from
  the exception. A non-Failure
  exception is a worker bug — its
  traceback goes into the log.
end note

group single transaction
    Worker -> Database: SELECT status, claimed_by\nFOR UPDATE
    activate Database
    Database --> Worker: row

    alt still RUNNING and still ours
        Worker -> Database: UPDATE tasks\n{status: FAILED,\nfinished_at: utcnow(),\nlease_until: NULL,\nlogs: logs + error + commit,\noutputs: partial outputs}
        Worker -> Database: INSERT task_events\n{type: task-failed,\ntask_id, task_type,\nfailure_kind: worker_failure}
    else the reaper already failed it
        Worker -> Database: UPDATE tasks\n(result columns only,\nstatus left untouched)
        note right
          The lease was taken over; the
          results are still worth keeping,
          the status is not ours to set.
        end note
    end
    deactivate Worker
    Database --> Database: COMMIT
end

Database -->> Backend: NOTIFY task_events\n+ NOTIFY task_finished
activate Backend

Backend --> Frontend: event: failed\n{failure_kind: worker_failure}
Frontend --> Frontend: show error, stop the\nprogress bar, offer retry

Backend -> Backend: task_finalizer.finalize_task()
deactivate Database

Backend -> Database: SELECT task\nWHERE finalized_at IS NULL\nFOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
activate Database
note right
  Every uvicorn process hears
  task_finished; SKIP LOCKED makes
  sure only one of them does the
  follow-up work.
end note
Database --> Backend: claimed task

Backend -> Database: UPDATE tasks\n{finalized_at: utcnow()}\n+ delete events of earlier tasks
note right
  A failed task sends no access mails
  and is not soft-deleted — the
  deployment stays visible with its
  log so the user can read what broke.
end note
Database --> Backend: committed
deactivate Database
deactivate Backend

== Case 2: the worker disappears (lease expires) ==

activate Worker
Worker -> Database: lease renewal every\nWORKER_LEASE_SECONDS / 3
activate Database
Database --> Worker: renewed
deactivate Database
note right of Worker
  The worker was killed, crashed or
  lost its database connection, so the
  renewals stop.
end note
destroy Worker

Backend -> Backend: run_reaper()\nevery TASK_REAPER_INTERVAL_SECONDS
activate Backend

Backend -> Database: SELECT tasks\nWHERE status = RUNNING\nAND lease_until < now()\nFOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED\nLIMIT 20
activate Database
Database --> Backend: expired tasks

loop for each expired task
    Backend -> Database: UPDATE tasks\n{status: FAILED,\nfinished_at: utcnow(),\nlease_until: NULL,\nlogs: logs + worker-lost message\n(in the task's locale)}
    Backend -> Database: INSERT task_events\n{type: task-failed,\nfailure_kind: worker_lost}
end
Database --> Database: COMMIT
Database -->> Backend: NOTIFY task_events\n+ NOTIFY task_finished
deactivate Database

Backend --> Frontend: event: failed\n{failure_kind: worker_lost}
Frontend --> Frontend: close the live stream,\nshow "worker lost"

Backend -> Backend: finalize_pending()\n(safety net each tick)
deactivate Backend

== Case 3: the state cannot be saved ==

activate Worker
Worker -> Backend: POST /internal/tfstate/{deployment_id}\n(OpenTofu http backend)
activate Backend
Backend --> Worker: connection error / 5xx
deactivate Backend
note right of Worker
  The API was unreachable at the end
  of an apply, past OpenTofu's own
  retries, so OpenTofu writes
  errored.tfstate. The resources it
  lists exist in OpenStack, so the
  file must not be lost with the
  job directory.
end note

Worker -> Worker: _preserve(errored.tfstate)
note right
  Fernet-encrypted copy into
  WORKER_STATE_RESCUE_DIR (a volume),
  written before any retry so it
  survives the worker dying.
end note

loop until WORKER_STATE_RESCUE_SECONDS, backoff 5s..60s
    Worker -> Backend: tofu state push errored.tfstate
    activate Backend
    note right
      Same task, same token — the backend
      lets a task override its own
      leftover lock, so the worker is not
      locked out by the lock it could
      never release.
    end note
    Backend -> Database: tf_state_store.write()\n(encrypted)
    activate Database
    Database --> Backend: stored
    deactivate Database
    Backend --> Worker: 200 OK
    deactivate Backend
end

alt push succeeded
    Worker -> Worker: delete the rescue copy\n+ log "state saved after all"
else still unreachable
    Worker -> Worker: log the copy's path and the\nrestore_tfstate.py command
    note right
      An admin restores it with
      scripts/restore_tfstate.py; the
      backend refuses a state of another
      lineage or an older serial unless
      --force is given.
    end note
end
deactivate Worker

@enduml
